{#-
  CowSwap Milkman — submit price-protected swap orders, priced against a pinned
  Uniswap V3 pool route (variant of milkman.tmpl for tokens with no usable
  Chainlink feed on mainnet, e.g. PENDLE).

  Uses the UniV3 DynamicSlippageChecker (aliases.curator.univ3_price_checker):
  the same DynamicSlippageChecker wrapper as the Chainlink variant, but its
  expected-out calculator (UniV3ExpectedOutCalculator) quotes a Uniswap V3 pool
  route via a static quoter instead of reading Chainlink feeds. Its
  priceCheckerData is ABI-encoded as (uint256 slippageBps, bytes innerData),
  where innerData is abi.encode(address[] swapPath, uint24[] poolFees) — the
  pool route the slippage check measures the swap against.

  UNITS — poolFees are in BIPS, not Uniswap fee units: a 0.3% pool is 30 (not
  3000), 0.05% is 5, 0.01% is 1. The calculator multiplies by 100 into
  Uniswap's hundredths-of-a-bip internally. The template rejects at render any
  fee outside {1, 5, 30, 100} — the factory's enabled tiers in bips — so most
  unit mistakes (3000, 500, 10000, 0) fail fast instead of pointing at a
  nonexistent pool the quoter would revert on (fail-closed but broken: funds
  sit in Milkman escrow until cancelled through the Safe). The one value
  validation CANNOT disambiguate is 100: as bips it is the 1% tier, as a raw
  Uniswap unit it would mean the 0.01% tier, and both pools often exist —
  writing 100 while thinking in raw units silently prices against the 1% pool,
  typically far thinner than intended, which undercuts the depth the
  manipulation-cost argument below depends on. If you mean the 0.01% tier,
  write 1. (Should Uniswap governance ever enable a new fee tier, the allowed
  set in the guard below needs the matching bips value added.)

  Pinning innerData is load-bearing, exactly as in milkman.tmpl: the slippage
  cap is a bound relative to whatever the route quotes. If innerData were left
  free, a compromised role member could quote through a worthless pool route
  (expectedOut ≈ 0), so "lose no more than slippageBps" would permit swapping
  the Safe's tokens for ~nothing and still clear the gate.

  SPOT, NOT TWAP — the calculator quotes the pool route's CURRENT state at
  settlement time. Unlike the Chainlink variant, the reference price can be
  moved within the settlement block by trading against the pinned pools. The
  residual exposure is bounded and priced:
    - loss per order is capped at slippageBps × order size, whatever happens
      to the pools;
    - moving the pinned route past the cap costs the manipulator real slippage
      plus LP fees against the pools' in-range depth, and CoW settlement is
      competitive — a solver attempting it is bidding against honest solvers;
    - so keep clips small relative to the pinned pools' depth: set
      max_approval so that cap × clip is not worth the manipulation cost.
  When a usable Chainlink feed exists for the pair, prefer milkman.tmpl — an
  external oracle reference is strictly harder to move than a pool.

  Note the swapPath is a PRICING route only: the actual swap is settled by CoW
  solvers on whatever venue wins; intermediate path tokens never touch the
  Safe. Only path[0] (fromToken) and path[-1] (toToken) move.

  Required params:
    swaps — list of allowed swaps, each pinning its own pricing route and cap:
              - path: [<TOKEN key>, ...]   # ≥ 2 token alias keys; first is the
                                           # fromToken, last is the toToken
                fees: [<int>, ...]         # pool fee per hop, in BIPS (see
                                           # UNITS above); length = path − 1
                max_slippage_bps: <int>    # UNQUOTED integer; e.g. 200 ≡ ≤ 2%
            One `or` branch per swap, with the cap and route bound to the exact
            (from, to) pair.

  Optional params:
    max_approval — exclusive upper bound (in base units) for the approve
                   `amount` on every from-token, emitted as `less_than
                   max_approval`. Defaults to uint256.max, which only rules out
                   the literal infinite-approval sentinel and does NOT bound
                   exposure. Under a spot-quoted checker this bound is part of
                   the security argument (see SPOT, NOT TWAP): set it so a
                   single clip is small against the pinned pools' depth. A
                   single value applies to all from-tokens, so it is most
                   precise with one from-token; with mixed decimals, pick a
                   bound valid for each.

  Policy enforced:
    approve(spender=Milkman, amount < max_approval) on each from-token
      (path[0] of each swap, deduplicated).
    requestSwapExactTokensForTokens, per swap branch:
      amountIn     pass (bounded operationally by the approve ceiling)
      fromToken    == aliases.tokens[path[0]]
      toToken      == aliases.tokens[path[-1]]
      to           == avatar (proceeds stay in the Safe)
      appData      pass (CoW Protocol order metadata, set at runtime)
      priceChecker == aliases.curator.univ3_price_checker
      priceCheckerData → abi_encoded:
        slippageBps  < max_slippage_bps + 1   (i.e. ≤ max_slippage_bps)
        innerData    == abi.encode(path addresses, fees)
                                                  (the pool route is pinned, so
                                                   the cap is measured against a
                                                   fixed route, not a
                                                   caller-chosen one)

    Note: cancelSwap is NOT included. Milkman's cancelSwap targets the per-swap
    order clone (address unknown at policy-creation time), so it cannot be
    pre-authorised; cancellations are executed directly through the Safe UI.
-#}
{#- Fail fast on malformed swaps: emitting an undefined variable throws under
    throwOnUndefined, pointing at the offending guard line. -#}
{%- for swap in swaps -%}
  {%- if (swap.path | length) < 2 -%}
    {{ milkman_univ3_error_path_needs_at_least_two_tokens }}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if (swap.fees | length) + 1 != (swap.path | length) -%}
    {{ milkman_univ3_error_fees_length_must_be_path_length_minus_one }}
  {%- endif -%}
  {#- Must be an UNQUOTED integer: nunjucks `+` concatenates strings, so a
      quoted "200" would render the less_than ceiling as "2001" (a 10× more
      permissive cap), and a missing value would render NaN. -#}
  {%- if swap.max_slippage_bps is not number -%}
    {{ milkman_univ3_error_max_slippage_bps_must_be_an_unquoted_integer }}
  {%- endif -%}
  {#- Fees must be UNQUOTED members of the enabled UniV3 tiers in BIPS (see
      UNITS in the header). This turns raw-Uniswap-unit mistakes (3000, 500,
      10000) into render errors; it cannot disambiguate 100 (1% tier in bips,
      0.01% tier in raw units) — that one is on the author. -#}
  {%- for fee in swap.fees -%}
    {%- if fee not in [1, 5, 30, 100] -%}
      {{ milkman_univ3_error_fee_must_be_a_univ3_tier_in_bips_1_5_30_or_100 }}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{#- Deduplicate the from-token keys (path[0] of each swap) for the approves. -#}
{%- set from_keys = [] -%}
{%- for swap in swaps -%}
  {%- if (swap.path | first) not in from_keys -%}
    {%- set _ = from_keys.push(swap.path | first) -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
roles:
{%- for token in from_keys %}
  - address: "{{ aliases.tokens[token] }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function approve(address spender, uint256 amount)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: spender
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to"
            value: "{{ aliases.curator.milkman }}"
            value_type: "address"
          - name: amount
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "less_than"
            value: "{{ max_approval | default('115792089237316195423570985008687907853269984665640564039457584007913129639935') }}"
            value_type: "uint256"
{%- endfor %}

  - address: "{{ aliases.curator.milkman }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function requestSwapExactTokensForTokens(uint256 amountIn, address fromToken, address toToken, address to, bytes32 appData, address priceChecker, bytes priceCheckerData)"
        execution_options: "none"
        operator: "or"
        branches:
{%- for swap in swaps %}
{%- set path_addrs = [] -%}
{%- for key in swap.path -%}
  {%- set _ = path_addrs.push(aliases.tokens[key]) -%}
{%- endfor %}
          - operator: "matches"
            params:
              - name: amountIn
                operator: "pass"
              - name: fromToken
                operator: "equal_to"
                value: "{{ aliases.tokens[swap.path | first] }}"
                value_type: "address"
              - name: toToken
                operator: "equal_to"
                value: "{{ aliases.tokens[swap.path | last] }}"
                value_type: "address"
              - name: to
                operator: "equal_to_avatar"
              - name: appData
                operator: "pass"
              - name: priceChecker
                operator: "equal_to"
                value: "{{ aliases.curator.univ3_price_checker }}"
                value_type: "address"
              - name: priceCheckerData
                param_type: "abi_encoded"
                children:
                  - name: slippageBps
                    param_type: "static"
                    operator: "less_than"
                    value: "{{ swap.max_slippage_bps + 1 }}"
                    value_type: "uint256"
                  - name: innerData
                    param_type: "dynamic"
                    operator: "equal_to"
                    value: "{{ [path_addrs, swap.fees] | abi_encode(['address[]', 'uint24[]']) }}"
                    value_type: "bytes"
                    # display-only: lets `zac plan` decode the pinned blob back to
                    # (swapPath, poolFees) instead of printing opaque hex.
                    display_decode:
                      - { name: swapPath, type: "address[]" }
                      - { name: poolFees, type: "uint24[]" }
{%- endfor %}
